cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite the accompanying paper (preferred-citation below)."
title: "TCCB: Therapeutic Challenge Competence Benchmark"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-05-06"
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  TCCB (Therapeutic Challenge Competence Benchmark) is a skill-specific
  calibration benchmark for one therapeutic intervention — Hill's Challenge
  (Helping Skills System Category 6). It comprises 170 single-turn clinical
  scenarios (120 Challenge-prescribed across four thematic clusters and 50
  validation-appropriate controls), the prompts used to elicit and judge
  responses, 1,000 responses produced by claude-opus-4-6, and 3,000
  classifications produced by three cross-family LLM judges (Claude Haiku,
  Gemini 2.5 Flash, DeepSeek-Chat). It accompanies the ICAIMH 2026 paper
  "Token Mimicry or Therapeutic Competence? Testing LLMs Against Hill's
  Challenge Skill in Mental Health Support Scenarios."
